    "name_raw": "Steam Spell",
    "definition_type_raw": "Metamagic",
    "source_book_raw": "Aquatic Adventures pg. 59",
    "definition_raw": "Source Aquatic Adventures pg. 59\nYou’ve built off of some of the closely-guarded secrets of the undine steamcasters, allowing you to use fire magic underwater easily.\n\nBenefit: You can apply Steam Spell only to a spell with the fire descriptor. A steam spell works underwater without a caster level check, but it requires a caster level check to function above water. A steam spell uses up a slot the same spell level as the spell’s actual level.",
